  // the whole viewport so the game legitimately gains/loses that width; windowed, the window itself grows or
  // shrinks by the same amount instead -- which is what real applications do, and what keeps the canvas on
  // its exact integer scale rather than dropping to a fractional one the moment a panel opens.
